==English==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} ''[[#Old French|malison]]'', from {{etyl|la}} ''[[maledictio]]'', from the past participle stem of ''[[maledicere]]'', from {{term|male||badly}} + {{term|dicere||say}}.  Compare ''[[malediction]]''.

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|/ˈmælɪzən/, /ˈmælɪsən/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[curse]].
#:*'''1819''': “A hide of land I give to thee in my steads of Walbrugham, from me and mine to thee and thine aye and for ever; and God’s '''malison''' on his head who this gainsays!” — Walter Scott, ''Ivanhoe''

